WEBVTT

00:06.615 --> 00:08.399
Wait, wait.
You're listening... 

00:08.486 --> 00:09.966
- Okay?
- All right.

00:10.053 --> 00:12.969
- Okay?
- All right.

00:13.056 --> 00:14.318
- You're listening...
- Listening...

00:14.405 --> 00:16.190
...to Radiolab.

00:16.277 --> 00:17.974
Radiolab.
- From...

00:18.061 --> 00:19.628
- WNYC.
- C.

00:19.671 --> 00:20.759
- C?
- Yup.

00:20.846 --> 00:22.544
And NPR.

00:24.372 --> 00:25.851
I've learned...
How would you describe this on?

00:25.895 --> 00:29.899
My sense is
that you walk into a wild plac.

00:29.942 --> 00:32.075
Then you hear the wind
and the trees,

00:32.119 --> 00:35.557
and you hear these chirps
and sounds and calls,

00:35.600 --> 00:38.299
and they're just part of the...
they're part of the wild.

00:38.299 --> 00:42.303
They're wildlife, but there's
now a group of scientists

00:42.346 --> 00:44.783
- who listen much more closely

00:44.870 --> 00:47.438
and who are reducing wildlife
to wild talk.

00:47.482 --> 00:49.440
- It's-it's, uh...
Yeah.

00:49.484 --> 00:51.964
There are words in there.

00:52.008 --> 00:55.098
When you find the words,
as the people we will meet do

00:55.142 --> 00:57.883
in these stories, you end up
not just understanding

00:57.927 --> 01:00.669
but actually entering that
wild space in a very cool way.

01:00.669 --> 01:02.323
- Right.
- Yes.

01:02.323 --> 01:03.454
Or as a dolphin might say...

01:03.498 --> 01:04.455
How would a dolphin say it?

01:04.499 --> 01:05.674
I don't know.

01:05.674 --> 01:07.545
Well, then, then you know what?

01:07.545 --> 01:09.243
That is exactly kind of the
question of this next segment.

01:09.286 --> 01:11.027
I mean, the dream
that a human being

01:11.114 --> 01:12.811
can talk to a dolphin
or any animal...

01:12.898 --> 01:14.509
- Sorry?
- Your order.

01:14.552 --> 01:16.511
Sir, you can get back in line.

01:16.598 --> 01:18.817
Bae, whatever.

01:18.904 --> 01:20.471
It's all right.
You could go, or...

01:20.471 --> 01:22.691
Nah, it's whatever.

01:22.734 --> 01:24.606
Go ahead.

01:26.738 --> 01:28.044
Could I get a large coffee,
please?

01:28.088 --> 01:29.698
Mm-hmm. Is that all?

01:29.698 --> 01:32.222
Yeah. Thanks.

02:31.977 --> 02:34.241
Katie, he's here.

02:34.328 --> 02:36.982
- She's coming.
- Great. Thanks.

02:41.073 --> 02:43.728
Are you using the, um,

02:43.772 --> 02:46.035
the standing lamp?

02:46.078 --> 02:48.777
The-the shaker beige one
in the guest room?

02:48.820 --> 02:50.605
No, not really.

02:50.648 --> 02:53.216
Uh, any chance
I could borrow it?

02:53.216 --> 02:55.784
I-I could use a little bit
more light in my place, and...

02:55.827 --> 02:59.004
- Hey, Dad.
- Hey, kiddo.

02:59.048 --> 03:01.790
All right.
I'll-I'll just grab it later?

03:01.833 --> 03:04.706
- Sure, that's fine.
- Okay.

03:04.793 --> 03:07.361
All right, let's do it.
How you doing?

03:07.404 --> 03:10.146
- I'm good.
- That's nice.

03:10.233 --> 03:11.843
...substantially impact
racial matters

03:11.887 --> 03:13.932
- in modern day society.
Well, yes.

03:14.019 --> 03:15.934
In the case of the Tesla trial,

03:16.021 --> 03:18.589
you have a Black man suing
Josh Beckford,

03:18.676 --> 03:21.288
an early investor at Tesla,
due to the fact

03:21.331 --> 03:23.159
that his ancestors were enslavd

03:23.159 --> 03:25.466
by relatives of Mr. Beckford's.

03:25.466 --> 03:28.033
That human capital and profit
can be directly linked

03:28.077 --> 03:29.818
to the financials
of the company,

03:29.818 --> 03:33.082
so I do think there's merit,
and he could win the lawsuit.

03:33.125 --> 03:34.823
Not could win. Did win.

03:34.823 --> 03:36.825
Mr. Mbaye did win the lawsuit,

03:36.825 --> 03:40.263
a scenario that seemed
impossible to many beforehand.

03:40.263 --> 03:42.483
And you have to think
this decision will have

03:42.526 --> 03:44.615
very far-reaching consequences
all around the world...

03:44.659 --> 03:46.095
- Dad?
- especially in America due...

03:46.182 --> 03:47.836
Yeah, sweetie?

03:47.879 --> 03:49.968
Mom sprayed herself
with that flower perfume

03:50.012 --> 03:51.535
before you picked me up.

03:54.843 --> 03:56.584
I think she wants you
to come home.

03:58.063 --> 04:00.327
Did she say that?

04:01.632 --> 04:04.418
No. I just think so.

04:08.030 --> 04:10.554
Okay. Got it.

04:21.652 --> 04:24.220
All right, have a good day
at school, sweetie.

04:27.310 --> 04:29.051
The Marvin Gaye
versus Robin Thicke...

04:29.094 --> 04:30.618
Hey, Dad?

04:30.661 --> 04:32.228
Yeah.

04:32.272 --> 04:35.362
Can you stay over
at Mom's soon?

04:36.667 --> 04:40.497
You know what?
I'll talk to her about it.

04:45.023 --> 04:48.026
Don't you think this might
actually heighten tensions

04:48.113 --> 04:49.593
between Black and white people?

04:49.680 --> 04:53.684
- It feels divisive...

04:53.728 --> 04:56.383
The Tesla investor
was the owner

04:56.426 --> 04:57.949
of this Black man's ancestor.

04:57.993 --> 04:59.821
So, also the owner
of that man's future.

04:59.908 --> 05:02.476
You're right. It's-it's never
gonna be solved easily.

05:38.947 --> 05:41.950
Can you believe this guy?

05:41.950 --> 05:44.082
Now this Tesla exec owes him
a ton of money.

05:44.082 --> 05:47.434
He'll be set for life.

05:52.395 --> 05:54.528
This whole thing is crazy.

05:57.357 --> 06:00.577
Do you even care? It's unfair.

06:00.621 --> 06:03.101
Uh, whatever.

06:03.188 --> 06:05.321
I mean, it's not like he's even
gonna notice. He's rich.

06:10.587 --> 06:12.328
We're meeting.

06:12.328 --> 06:14.765
Uh, what for?

06:22.382 --> 06:24.601
Come on in.

06:24.645 --> 06:26.995
All right, I think
that's everybody.

06:27.038 --> 06:29.867
As some of you might have heard,

06:29.911 --> 06:33.131
I did get word from the CEO
and head executives

06:33.218 --> 06:35.133
that we'll be having
some layoffs.

06:36.787 --> 06:38.789
How soon?

06:38.833 --> 06:40.356
We'll get into that later today.

06:40.400 --> 06:42.271
I've been told that HR will...

06:42.358 --> 06:43.403
This is ridiculous!

06:46.797 --> 06:49.844
Now, I know a lot of you
will have many questions,

06:49.887 --> 06:52.455
and we want to be sure
and answer all of 'em,

06:52.455 --> 06:54.414
but at this point in time,
that's all

06:54.457 --> 06:56.503
the information I have.

07:11.779 --> 07:14.259
There's a rumor they're being
sued with the same clause

07:14.303 --> 07:16.305
that got the Tesla guy.

07:16.348 --> 07:17.524
This shit's bonkers, right?

07:19.177 --> 07:21.484
Bonkers.

07:21.484 --> 07:23.834
Well, and it's cleared the way
for personal litigation now.

07:23.834 --> 07:25.967
They can just look you up
and force you to pay.

07:27.272 --> 07:28.970
What? No.

07:29.013 --> 07:31.276
- Really?
- Yeah.

07:31.320 --> 07:34.497
It's scary. I'm looking
at my family tree right now

07:34.497 --> 07:35.672
to make sure I'm in the clear.

07:35.716 --> 07:37.544
Everybody else is, too.

07:43.767 --> 07:46.074
- Lucky them.

07:46.074 --> 07:49.643
Not a care in the world.

07:49.643 --> 07:51.862
Aren't you worried?

07:51.906 --> 07:56.084
Nah. I don't yell "fire"
unless I see flames.

07:56.127 --> 07:57.433
There's no smoke on my end.

08:02.525 --> 08:04.875
You gonna check your background?

08:04.919 --> 08:07.095
Nah. I never signed up
for that stuff.

08:07.138 --> 08:09.097
Oh, you don't have to.

08:09.140 --> 08:10.577
One of your relatives
could have signed up.

08:10.664 --> 08:12.579
I can show you how to look.

08:12.666 --> 08:15.146
I'm fine.

08:15.190 --> 08:19.716
All... good.

08:44.349 --> 08:46.047
Mm, shout-out to his lawyer.

08:46.134 --> 08:48.571
- This is crazy, right?
It's crazy.

08:48.571 --> 08:50.834
He's got to put his money
where his mouth is now.

08:50.921 --> 08:52.575
- So what you gonna do

08:52.575 --> 08:54.359
- with your apolo-cheese?
Oh.

08:54.403 --> 08:57.145
No more apologies,
just apolo-cheese.

08:57.188 --> 09:00.017
Apolo-cheese! I like that.

09:00.061 --> 09:04.065
I'm gonna hit the mall and sped
some of this apolo-cheese!

09:04.108 --> 09:07.372
Yeah. Uh, you better get
some Nike stock, though, right?

09:07.416 --> 09:10.158
Okay? I'm about to go hire
that same lawyer.

09:10.201 --> 09:12.856
I'm sure somebody owes me
about $50 million.

09:12.900 --> 09:14.379
Mm-hmm, this is se...

09:24.564 --> 09:27.001
You got a lot of homework today?

09:27.044 --> 09:29.525
No, not too much.

09:29.569 --> 09:31.571
Well, that's good.

09:33.181 --> 09:35.096
You tired?

09:35.096 --> 09:37.620
No, not really.

09:42.756 --> 09:46.107
I'm thinking spaghetti
for dinner tonight.

09:46.194 --> 09:48.109
Huh? Maybe a little
of my famous garlic bread?

09:48.152 --> 09:49.806
Are we racist?

09:49.850 --> 09:52.417
What?

09:52.417 --> 09:54.332
A kid at school said
we're racist.

09:57.292 --> 10:01.470
That's not true, Katie.
That's...

10:04.734 --> 10:09.913
Right now,
Black people are just...

10:10.000 --> 10:12.786
Don't listen to that kid
at school, okay?

10:12.829 --> 10:14.701
You are not racist.

10:17.094 --> 10:19.053
Were we slave owners?

10:21.882 --> 10:24.798
No, we... Do you see any slaves
in our backyard?

10:24.841 --> 10:26.843
Mr. Pedro.

10:26.887 --> 10:29.585
Mr. Pe...?
No, I pay Mr. Pedro.

10:30.891 --> 10:32.893
You...

10:32.936 --> 10:35.286
Listen, that stuff happened
a long, long time ago.

10:35.330 --> 10:37.593
All right?
We-We're Austro-Hungarian.

10:37.680 --> 10:39.595
We were enslaved
during the Byzantine Empire.

10:39.682 --> 10:43.686
Uh, what? Should I fly
to Hungary and demand money now?

10:43.730 --> 10:45.166
That would be ridiculous, right?

10:46.820 --> 10:48.952
Right?

10:58.483 --> 11:00.703
Sweetie, dinner's ready.

11:05.012 --> 11:08.493
Hey.

11:08.493 --> 11:11.061
All right. Let's do it.

11:11.061 --> 11:12.628
Want cheese?

11:12.672 --> 11:14.674
Tell me when to stop.

11:18.112 --> 11:19.853
Mm-hmm.

11:24.074 --> 11:26.642
Ugh.

11:26.642 --> 11:28.470
Dig in.

11:50.231 --> 11:52.276
Eat.

11:58.892 --> 12:01.111
Marshall Johnson?

12:01.155 --> 12:02.896
Yes?

12:02.939 --> 12:05.333
You've been served.

12:10.251 --> 12:12.079
- I'm sorry. What is this about?

12:15.343 --> 12:18.999
My name is Sheniqua Johnson
of the St. Louis Johnsons.

12:19.042 --> 12:21.697
Your family owned
my great-great-grandmother

12:21.741 --> 12:23.394
and father for 12 years.

12:23.438 --> 12:25.048
You owe me money.

12:26.354 --> 12:30.227
Uh... I...

12:30.227 --> 12:32.926
There... there-there must be
some kind of mistake.

12:33.013 --> 12:36.233
Uh, you know, can we just
talk about this outside?

12:36.233 --> 12:37.713
- Uh-uh. There ain't been
no mistake.
- Excuse me.

12:37.800 --> 12:39.149
- Ooh, look what we got here.
- Excuse me!

12:39.149 --> 12:40.847
- Who is it, Dad?
- Uh, ma'am?
- Now, we got

12:40.934 --> 12:43.153
- one, two, three bedrooms.
- Uh...

12:43.240 --> 12:44.589
- Look at this bathroom.
- Uh, ma'am, could you...
could you

12:44.633 --> 12:46.504
- please get out of my house?
- They got that good stuff
in here.

12:46.591 --> 12:48.071
- Oh.
- Excuse me!

12:48.158 --> 12:50.160
You know what?
You owe me about $3 million.

12:50.204 --> 12:52.728
Ma'am, hey, hey, hey,
hey, stop it!

12:52.728 --> 12:54.512
Get out of my house!

12:54.599 --> 12:56.732
Uh-uh. This is my house,

12:56.819 --> 12:58.603
and I'm livestreaming
the entire thing.

12:58.603 --> 13:00.867
I want what's owed
to me, Marshall.

13:00.954 --> 13:03.304
You know what?

13:03.347 --> 13:05.436
- If you don't get out right now,
I'm calling the police.
- Hmm.

13:05.480 --> 13:08.222
- I'm calling the police
right now!
- You know what?

13:08.265 --> 13:10.311
Your family's got blood
on its hands.

13:10.398 --> 13:12.617
And don't bother
calling the police

13:12.661 --> 13:14.532
because I already been there.

13:16.839 --> 13:20.625
Ooh! Now,
Jamal's gonna love this spot.

13:20.669 --> 13:23.150
And don't slam my door!

13:31.027 --> 13:32.072
Uh-oh.

13:33.073 --> 13:35.031
Maybe...

13:35.075 --> 13:37.947
don't tell your mother
about this.

13:55.225 --> 13:57.793
Okay, let's do it.

13:57.837 --> 13:59.795
Here we go. Hold on. W-Wait...

13:59.839 --> 14:01.928
Just wait for me.

14:02.015 --> 14:04.017
Okay.

14:05.105 --> 14:07.368
Okay. All right, come on.

14:07.455 --> 14:09.370
Let's do it.

14:09.370 --> 14:11.415
Let's go.

14:25.821 --> 14:28.128
Hey.

14:28.171 --> 14:30.608
- Where's...?
- All the Black people?

14:30.695 --> 14:34.438
Besides Willy and Lester,
they didn't come in today.

14:39.052 --> 14:42.838
Did... did you get
your results back?

14:42.882 --> 14:46.711
69% Ashkenazi Jew, baby.

14:46.755 --> 14:49.062
You're Jew...?
Uh, you're Jewish?

14:49.105 --> 14:51.064
The world can finally know.

14:51.107 --> 14:53.109
We were slaves, too.

14:56.199 --> 14:58.723
Austro-Hungarians were slaves
as well.

14:59.724 --> 15:02.162
Come on, Marshall.

15:02.162 --> 15:03.990
That was like
a million years ago.

15:45.553 --> 15:50.688
Hey, um, the guy, uh,
with the shirt, uh...?

15:52.342 --> 15:54.823
- Oh,
Tim in Accounting?
- He... yeah.

15:54.866 --> 15:59.349
Yeah, the, um,
Black family suing him decided

15:59.436 --> 16:01.438
that they just wanted him
to acknowledge it,

16:01.438 --> 16:03.005
so he's got to wear that shirt
twice a week.

16:04.137 --> 16:07.488
One of them has to be Sunday.

16:07.575 --> 16:09.229
I don't know. Personally,

16:09.272 --> 16:11.144
I-I think he got off
kind of easy.

16:14.799 --> 16:16.801
Marshall Johnson,

16:16.801 --> 16:18.934
- you owe me money.
- No.

16:19.021 --> 16:21.415
- No.
- $3 million,
and you have to pay up.

16:21.458 --> 16:23.156
What do we want?
Compensation.

16:23.156 --> 16:26.855
- No.
- When do we want it? Now.

16:26.898 --> 16:29.249
Marshall Johnson's
great-great-granddaddy enslaved

16:29.249 --> 16:33.514
my great-great-granddaddy, and
he owes me a lifetime of pay!

16:33.601 --> 16:35.211
- No.

16:35.255 --> 16:38.519
No, no, no, no. No. No. No. No.

16:38.519 --> 16:40.086
Pay up!

16:40.173 --> 16:42.088
- Marshall Johnson.

16:42.175 --> 16:44.220
- Hey, excuse me.
- Paging Marshall Johnson.

16:44.264 --> 16:46.179
- Hey, excuse me. Excuse me.
- Marshall.

16:46.222 --> 16:48.050
All right, all right,
listen, I work here.

16:48.050 --> 16:49.834
All right? You can't come
to my place of work.

16:49.834 --> 16:51.836
Marshall Johnson,
you owe me money.

16:51.880 --> 16:53.882
I-I'm not the Tesla guy.

16:53.925 --> 16:55.971
Okay? I don't have
that kind of money.

16:56.058 --> 16:57.581
How much money
do you make a year?

16:57.625 --> 16:59.235
What? Uh...

16:59.279 --> 17:01.063
- How much money

17:01.107 --> 17:04.414
do you people in there
make a year?

17:04.501 --> 17:06.982
- I bet you it's more than I do.
- Could you please--

17:07.069 --> 17:10.855
I'm begging you-- could you
please just leave me alone?

17:10.899 --> 17:15.860
That's exactly what
my great-great-grandmother said.

17:15.947 --> 17:17.906
- Marshall Johnson's
great-great-granddaddy

17:17.949 --> 17:20.039
- was a slave owner.
- No, no, no. Not true.

17:20.082 --> 17:23.433
He owned
my great-great-granddaddy.

17:23.433 --> 17:25.218
- Not true.
- You need to pay up!

17:25.261 --> 17:30.440
$3 million.
$3 million.

17:30.484 --> 17:32.790
What do we want? Compensation!

17:32.790 --> 17:35.097
When do we want it? Now!

17:35.141 --> 17:37.665
Marshall Johnson's
great-great-granddaddy

17:37.708 --> 17:39.623
enslaved
my great-great-granddaddy...

17:40.929 --> 17:45.238
Get me a new car,
get Sierra a new car.

17:45.238 --> 17:46.674
You gonna get a Cadillac
or one of them, uh,

17:46.717 --> 17:48.937
- those Cybertrucks?
- I don't know.

17:48.980 --> 17:51.113
You know,
Jamal can get a new phone.

17:51.113 --> 17:53.681
Get Tangy and Sierra's mom
a new place,

17:53.724 --> 17:55.900
'cause Lord knows I can't be
dealing with that anymore.

17:55.944 --> 17:59.034
- Her mama?
- You already...

17:59.121 --> 18:01.254
- Hey, Lester?

18:01.341 --> 18:03.256
Could I... could I talk
to you for a sec?

18:06.041 --> 18:07.738
- Yeah. What's up?

18:07.782 --> 18:09.740
Hey, man. How you doing?

18:09.784 --> 18:11.046
- Pretty good.
- Ain't no such thing

18:11.090 --> 18:13.179
as free labor, Marshall.

18:13.266 --> 18:16.704
Pay up!

18:16.747 --> 18:19.359
Uh... look,

18:19.359 --> 18:22.405
I know this is a crazy time
and everything,

18:22.449 --> 18:24.973
and, uh, I-I really don't
know what to do.

18:25.060 --> 18:27.758
Uh, no, thanks. Thank you.

18:27.845 --> 18:31.501
Um, I'm just a guy,

18:31.501 --> 18:33.503
you know, trying to get by.

18:33.547 --> 18:39.074
And I feel like this woman
is harassing me, you know?

18:39.074 --> 18:40.902
She's kind of ruining my life.

18:40.945 --> 18:43.209
Uh, so...

18:43.252 --> 18:46.864
I-I just don't know what to do.

18:46.951 --> 18:49.302
You honestly want my advice?

18:49.345 --> 18:51.304
Uh, yes.

18:51.347 --> 18:54.089
Look, man,
I grew up with Black women.

18:54.133 --> 18:56.091
Right. I figured.

18:56.178 --> 18:58.441
The only thing you can do is
say you were wrong

18:58.528 --> 19:00.443
and give her as much money
as you can.

19:00.530 --> 19:03.098
She'll probably want to meet
with you one-on-one,

19:03.098 --> 19:04.752
cut you down a bit...

19:04.795 --> 19:06.101
I just don't know what to do.

19:06.101 --> 19:08.538
- Hmm.
- Honestly, my advice?

19:08.582 --> 19:10.801
You got to fight that shit, man.

19:10.845 --> 19:12.673
Come in as hard as her.

19:12.716 --> 19:13.978
- It's the principle.

19:14.022 --> 19:15.763
I looked her up on Instagram.

19:15.763 --> 19:17.634
All she's talking
about is the fact

19:17.678 --> 19:19.549
- that you owe her a lot
of money.

19:19.593 --> 19:21.769
100% Nordic?!

19:21.769 --> 19:23.597
How is that even
fucking possible?

19:25.773 --> 19:28.384
This concerns all of us,
Willy.

19:28.428 --> 19:31.257
No, it don't, Ashley.

19:33.911 --> 19:35.696
No, it don't.

19:48.709 --> 19:50.798
What?

20:11.862 --> 20:13.864
Uh, I was supposed
to pick her up.

20:13.908 --> 20:15.736
What's going on?

20:17.651 --> 20:19.609
Is it true?

20:19.653 --> 20:22.264
Is wh...?

20:22.264 --> 20:25.833
Oh, my God.
Was Sheniqua here?

20:25.876 --> 20:27.835
Did, did she talk to you?

20:27.878 --> 20:29.967
- Marshall, I can't believe you.
- Okay.

20:30.054 --> 20:32.405
Let's just go inside
and discuss this.

20:32.448 --> 20:34.058
Look, you can't come in here.

20:34.102 --> 20:35.843
Seriously, Natalie?

20:38.280 --> 20:40.064
Have you checked
your background?

20:40.108 --> 20:41.936
This could have
easily happened to you.

20:41.936 --> 20:44.417
- I'm Peruvian.
This would never happen to me.
- Per...

20:44.460 --> 20:46.201
You were white yesterday!

20:46.245 --> 20:49.639
Okay, look, Natalie,

20:49.683 --> 20:53.556
please, can we just...
c-can we just go inside

20:53.600 --> 20:55.993
and just sit down
and-and just talk about...?

21:04.480 --> 21:08.789
Can I... can I say good night
to Katie?

21:09.790 --> 21:13.533
Marshall...

21:13.576 --> 21:15.448
I can't have my finances
take a hit.

21:18.189 --> 21:20.235
We have
to make the divorce official.

21:27.242 --> 21:28.896
Wait. What?

21:34.945 --> 21:37.644
This is not happening.

22:04.540 --> 22:06.716
What the...?

22:11.765 --> 22:14.202
- There he is!

22:14.245 --> 22:15.638
That's the guy right there.

22:15.725 --> 22:16.900
Oh.

22:16.944 --> 22:19.773
Go get him, Jason!

22:24.865 --> 22:27.084
No, no, no, no.

22:27.171 --> 22:29.652
Oh, shit, shit, shit, shit,
shit, shit, shit.

22:34.788 --> 22:36.529
Oh, my God.

22:37.051 --> 22:38.879
Shit, shit, shit, shit, shit.

22:40.837 --> 22:44.014
Oh, fuck. Oh, fuck. Oh.

22:54.198 --> 22:55.896
Well, sir, you know,
my time was wasted, too...

23:23.489 --> 23:26.709
We didn't do it, but we can
help you get your money.

23:26.753 --> 23:29.190
Don't know if you owe
restitution taxes?

23:29.233 --> 23:32.062
We can help you with that.

25:13.686 --> 25:17.124
Hi. Would you like something
to drink?

25:17.124 --> 25:21.171
Uh, uh, I'll just have
what he's having.

25:21.258 --> 25:22.825
Okay.

25:33.488 --> 25:35.185
How long are you here for?

25:35.229 --> 25:40.364
Honestly,
I am not quite even sure.

25:40.408 --> 25:43.498
Just checked in today.

25:45.587 --> 25:48.503
Yeah, I flew in a few days ago.

25:48.547 --> 25:50.592
Looking for a new place.

25:52.159 --> 25:55.075
They can't find my bag, though,
so I look like hell.

25:59.383 --> 26:02.517
Name's Earnest.
Friends call me "E."

26:04.563 --> 26:06.739
Marshall.

26:08.044 --> 26:10.873
I have a feeling we're
in the same boat, Marshall.

26:12.179 --> 26:14.660
You owe a lot?

26:17.053 --> 26:21.231
This woman-- she...

26:21.275 --> 26:23.320
follows me everywhere,

26:23.364 --> 26:26.802
won't leave me alone.

26:26.846 --> 26:29.109
- Thanks.
- You're welcome.

26:31.285 --> 26:35.681
Just... can't believe
this is actually happening.

26:39.728 --> 26:41.774
Two days ago,
I had a good life,

26:41.861 --> 26:44.777
and now I'm being fucked by
some shit that I didn't even do.

26:44.820 --> 26:48.258
I'm losing my wife, my house,

26:48.345 --> 26:50.347
my daughter.

26:50.347 --> 26:53.002
I don't know.

26:53.002 --> 26:54.917
Didn't fucking do anything.

27:10.237 --> 27:13.022
As I was saying, I don't know.

27:17.374 --> 27:19.420
What?

27:22.858 --> 27:25.513
I don't know.

27:28.690 --> 27:30.692
My grandfather used to tell me

27:30.692 --> 27:34.478
how his father built everything
we had from the ground up,

27:34.522 --> 27:38.395
pulled himself up
by his own bootstraps, you know?

27:39.396 --> 27:42.704
Turns out, he didn't.

27:42.748 --> 27:46.186
Turns out he had a lot of help.

27:46.273 --> 27:48.884
And a lot of kids.

27:52.148 --> 27:53.976
Maybe it's only right.

27:55.848 --> 27:59.982
E, we don't deserve this.

28:00.069 --> 28:02.245
Well, what do they deserve?

28:06.859 --> 28:08.904
We were treating slavery

28:08.948 --> 28:13.779
as if it were a mystery
buried in the past,

28:13.866 --> 28:17.434
something to investigate
if we chose to.

28:17.521 --> 28:21.438
And now that history has
a monetary value.

28:22.744 --> 28:27.444
Confession is not absolution.

28:29.098 --> 28:32.101
And in the case of this
person... What's her name?

28:32.145 --> 28:33.581
Sheniqua.

28:33.624 --> 28:38.107
To Sheniqua, to them...

28:38.151 --> 28:41.110
slavery is not past.

28:41.154 --> 28:44.679
I mean, it's not a mystery.

28:44.766 --> 28:48.248
It is not
an historical curiosity.

28:48.291 --> 28:50.554
It is a cruel,

28:50.598 --> 28:54.080
unavoidable ghost that haunts
in a way we can't see.

28:55.516 --> 28:57.866
None of us are perfect.

29:03.132 --> 29:05.918
So now you're what?
You're separated from your wife?

29:05.961 --> 29:08.050
She's taking your kid?

29:08.137 --> 29:10.836
Now she has to be raised
without a father?

29:10.923 --> 29:13.012
She has to build wealth

29:13.055 --> 29:15.928
and success
from the ground up, right?

29:15.971 --> 29:18.582
It's similar
to the position we put them in.

29:20.759 --> 29:23.762
But we're gonna be okay.

29:27.722 --> 29:30.333
Your daughter's gonna be okay.

29:32.596 --> 29:35.382
The curse has been lifted
from her.

29:37.297 --> 29:40.169
All of us--

29:40.169 --> 29:45.174
we were running from it,
but now we're free.

29:49.483 --> 29:51.311
Excuse me.

30:27.260 --> 30:29.436
Come on! Come on, babies!
Come on!

30:29.479 --> 30:31.438
You got it!

30:31.481 --> 30:33.919
Yeah!

30:34.006 --> 30:36.356
Ooh, I'm so proud
of my babies.

30:53.590 --> 30:55.897
Holy shit.

30:55.897 --> 30:57.856
There's more
where that came from.

32:18.980 --> 32:20.895
All right, guys, uh,

32:20.982 --> 32:22.984
I got a decent-sized reservation
in the main dining hall,

32:23.028 --> 32:25.030
so I'm gonna need
all hands on deck for that,

32:25.073 --> 32:27.423
full hands in, full hands out.
You know the routine.

32:27.423 --> 32:30.035
Uh, make sure to push
the daily specials, okay?

32:30.078 --> 32:31.906
I don't want to ask
about that again.

32:31.993 --> 32:34.778
And if anyone has a portion
of their paycheck going

32:34.778 --> 32:37.042
to restitution taxes,
stay after.

32:37.085 --> 32:38.913
Everyone else, hit the floor.

32:44.832 --> 32:47.400
Simon, ten percent?

32:47.443 --> 32:49.402
- One second, please.

32:49.445 --> 32:51.578
Okay, you're good. Thank you.

32:51.621 --> 32:53.580
- Hey.

32:53.623 --> 32:55.364
Uh, name of payee?

32:55.408 --> 32:57.366
Uh, Sheniqua Johnson.

32:57.410 --> 33:00.543
- Okay. And percentage?

33:00.587 --> 33:04.156
- 15%.
- 15%?

33:04.156 --> 33:06.201
Ouch.

33:07.594 --> 33:09.944
Well, at least
tips aren't garnished.

33:09.988 --> 33:12.033
There's that.

33:12.033 --> 33:14.862
- Uh, you're good.
- Cool. Thanks.

33:14.905 --> 33:16.777
And you're doing ten again?

33:31.009 --> 33:32.401
Basura blanca.

33:32.445 --> 33:33.663
Hey, huevón.

33:33.750 --> 33:35.448
Get to work.

33:35.491 --> 33:38.668
Te vi llegar tarde, pendejo.

33:38.755 --> 33:41.758
Ah!

33:41.802 --> 33:45.458
Okay. Keep talking like that,
they're gonna make you a busboy.

34:14.487 --> 34:17.403
All right, good evening,
ladies and gentlemen.

34:19.492 --> 34:22.321
- All right.

34:22.364 --> 34:24.236
- Hey.

34:30.111 --> 34:32.026
Okay.

34:33.636 --> 34:35.464
Ooh.
